course: dictionary
lesson: 10985
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. The word warning is a good example. As a noun, it can be a message that tells people about a danger: «Pain is a warning sign, so take breaks and stop if it hurts.» Here the pain is your body's message that something is wrong.
explain: Warning can also mean a message saying you will be punished if you do something again. «A police officer came round and gave him a warning.» The clue is that he did something wrong and was told not to do it again. This warning is about behaviour, not about danger.
explain: Warning is also the -ing form of the verb warn, as in «She is warning us about the ice.» Check the sentence: can you swap in "telling us" and still make sense? Yes, so warning works as a verb here. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to test it.
fact: A warning tells people about a danger or a problem so they can avoid it.
fact: A warning can also be a message that you will be punished if you do the same thing again.
fact: Warning is the -ing form of warn: warn, warns, warned, warning.
fact: «Hiss» means a sharp, long sound, and «A hiss is a cat's warning to stay away» means the cat is telling you to keep your distance.
fact: Warning labels on cleaning products and medicines tell you how to stay safe.
exercise: «The yellow triangle sign by the pool is a warning, so walk slowly.» What does warning mean here? | *Something that tells people about a danger | A song that the lifeguard sings | A prize for swimming the fastest | A bill for using the pool
exercise: «A hiss is a cat's warning to stay away.» What does the hiss tell you? | The cat wants its dinner | The cat is sleepy | The cat is very happy | *Keep your distance from the cat
exercise: «She is warning us about the ice.» Find and copy the word that is the -ing form of warn. | she | about | ice | *warning
test: «The referee's word is final: a yellow card is a warning, and the next mistake means a red card.» What kind of warning is a yellow card? | *A message that you will be punished if you do it again | A sign that says Danger | A cold drink for the player | A sound from a siren
test: «Heat exhaustion can turn into heatstroke; one warning sign is that a hot person stops sweating.» What is a warning sign here? | *Something that shows a serious problem may be coming | A cool breeze | A sweaty shirt | A hot drink
exam: «Pain is a warning sign, so take breaks.» Which meaning of warning is used here? | A message about a punishment | A sound that tells you a bell is ringing | *Something that tells you about a danger or a problem | A stick used to warn a dog
